# =============================================================================
# Environment variables
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local        # macOS / Linux
#   copy .env.example .env.local      # Windows
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored. This file IS committed — keep it as a template
# only, and never put a real key in it.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site URL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute origin used for canonical URLs, Open Graph tags and sitemap.xml.
# Must include the scheme. No trailing slash.
#
# On Vercel, set this in Project → Settings → Environment Variables for
# Production, Preview and Development, then redeploy.
#
# If unset, the app falls back to http://localhost:3000, which is correct for
# local development.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form — email delivery (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The /api/contact route works with NO configuration:
#
#   • RESEND_API_KEY unset  →  "log mode". Submissions are validated exactly as
#                              in production, then printed to the server console
#                              with console.info(). Nothing is sent. This is the
#                              intended local-development behaviour.
#
#   • RESEND_API_KEY set    →  the route POSTs to https://api.resend.com/emails
#                              directly (no SDK dependency) and returns a real
#                              success/failure to the form.
#
# To enable real delivery:
#   1. Create an account at https://resend.com
#   2. Add and verify your sending domain (or use their onboarding sender).
#   3. Create an API key and paste it below.
#   4. Restart the dev server, or redeploy on Vercel.
#
# SERVER-ONLY. The `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix is deliberately absent: this value must
# never be exposed to the browser.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Where contact submissions are delivered.
# Falls back to `contact.email` in src/data/profile.ts when unset.
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=you@example.com

# The "from" header. Must be an address on a domain you verified with Resend.
# While testing you can omit this and Resend's onboarding sender is used.
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=Website <onboarding@resend.dev>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# • Variables without the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix are only readable in server code
#   (route handlers, server components, `next.config.ts`). Referencing one in a
#   "use client" file will inline `undefined`.
# • Changing env vars requires a restart. Editing `.env.local` does not hot
#   reload the values.
